<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore non-oil exports rise 1.1 pct in October.</title>
<headline>Singapore non-oil exports rise 1.1 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports rose a nominal 1.1 percent year-on-year in October to Singapore $7.68 billion after falling 6.2 percent in September, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 15 financial institutions had predicted a nominal year-on-year fall of 1.4 percent in October.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports rose 5.6 percent in October to S$9.81 billion after falling 2.2 pct in September.  </p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				  October		  September</p>
<p>    Total trade	   32.06 (3.3)	    29.44 (-0.8)</p>
<p>    Exports		 15.70 (4.8)	    14.67 (-1.4)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports     9.03 (3.1)	     8.61 (-2.4)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.34 (15.9)	    1.31 (26.3)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  7.68 (1.1)	     7.30 (-6.2)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     6.68 (7.3)	     6.06 (nil)</p>
<p>    Imports		 16.35 (1.8)	    14.77 (-0.1)</p>
